":"1787102007924171001-b3fd1d5d-0ebf-48e6-bbf6-8337e6eba1b2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1e14c49e102225ba87f38d500144938a66d9a5504214e94f436dc404a0676421","event_uuid":"5437fbca-e7cc-4375-b1be-4d362a1440e5","position":{"commit_sha":"82d02be68f13de68bfb5bd86ef5011dbd8869c77","position":"1787102032505400001-5437fbca-e7cc-4375-b1be-4d362a1440e5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fef92d20d38f450d682ac32720d256367d380c793d9a016f64539fbc9f0af9e4","event_uuid":"afdbf58d-cf10-4e4a-9274-2d645f80186f","position":{"commit_sha":"9f7853d535847d1383a5be30efe9ba3cada37e16","position":"1787102491388367001-afdbf58d-cf10-4e4a-9274-2d645f80186f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6a5ce263bd351f7dccdd8953a4d1de9002f12094cd7985d9f13aaf7c22e38984","event_uuid":"e0eda35f-49c8-422f-9b0b-ac9dfaf18a80","position":{"commit_sha":"3c5d5677dee4eae81233f66ab728b1ab2e43b958","position":"1787103343406744001-e0eda35f-49c8-422f-9b0b-ac9dfaf18a80"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bf56f513c3aa06dd20edb98b0441194ad18ec6eca90fa91c2d389986453216c3","event_uuid":"3ee57c48-5945-48ec-88c5-7879d922812d","position":{"commit_sha":"fda2500acea378b28089a30d1087f3fbff9d8cd4","position":"1787103625079113001-3ee57c48-5945-48ec-88c5-7879d922812d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pilot cutover design (settled before implementation):\n\nClassification of the 3 legacy reads (all owner=composition per the gate — load_config, and os.environ.get with a DYNAMIC config-supplied env name → 'unresolved-env-read'):\n- mcp_server.py L422 (_mcp_gate), L591 (build_server cfg-None fallback), L735 (main): load_config() per-call/below-seam.\n- mcp_server.py L646: os.environ.get(mcp_cfg.auth_proxy_secret_env) — proxy secret at HTTP app-wrap time.\n- _mcp_auth.py L411 (introspection client_secret_env), L658 (build_composite_verifier proxy secret), L760 (_parse_static_record token_env): startup-time auth SECRET resolutions by config-named env var.\n\nRejected: the '# read-via:' marker — precedent (only in _config_schema.py, 12x) is documenting a config FIELD's read site, NOT suppressing consumer env reads. Not the intended owned-registration mechanism here.\n\nRejected: adding _mcp_auth.py to the gate's credential-boundary set — the reads classify as composition (unresolved dynamic name), not credential, so boundary ownership would not suppress them.\n\nChosen: genuine cut-to-seam. (1) Compose MCP config ONCE at server startup (main→build_server) and bind it so _mcp_gate/_readonly read the startup-bound value instead of load_config() per request. (2) Resolve the auth secret VALUES at that same startup composition (the boundary allowed to read env) and thread the resolved values into build_composite_verifier / the proxy-app wrap / static-token parsing, so _mcp_auth.py and mcp_server.py L646 no longer call os.environ.get. Then remove all 3 LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS entries; the gate (scan root src/rebar) must be clean. Behavioral oracle: tests/interfaces/facades MCP+auth suites + tests/interfaces/contracts MCP envelope + tests/unit/test_mcp_writes.py/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py (178 passing baseline; test_mcp_push_status.py excluded — pre-existing git-hooks env fixture flake, unrelated). Held-out seam-clean proof: tests/scripts/test_mcp_server_seam_clean_heldout.py.","timestamp":1787096785165688001}],"created_at":1787095126711798001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1df0ae3e-2e1e-47ed-9195-ebfbbb0dc840","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59ce-3ff1-b46a-4d8b"},{"link_uuid":"0411c164-1dee-46be-aa14-4b875ef0c46e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b464-181d-0ecb-45b9"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nSlice C1 (ticket 29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) recorded 3 below-seam ambient config/credential reads in the MCP server (mcp_server.py, _mcp_auth.py), incl. the deferred RP-04 S5 MCP load_config()-per-call cutover as entries in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS`. RP-04 is not complete while these ambient reads sit below the approved composition/credential/backend seams enforced by `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`. Parent: 075b-1479-dcb7-40ab.\n\nAffected files (relative to repo root):\n  - `src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py` (below-seam auth-secret reads cut to the seam)\n  - `src/rebar/mcp_server.py` (below-seam gate/config/proxy-secret reads cut to the seam)\n  - `src/rebar/config.py` (adds the three new owned composition-root resolvers this change introduces)\n  - `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py` (removes the drained MCP `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` rows)\n\n## Outcome\nEvery below-seam read in the two MCP files is CUT to compose through the approved composition-root seam. The chosen mechanism: this change ADDS three new owned composition-root resolvers to `config.py` (new `mcp_gate` / `compose_config` / `read_secret_env` helpers — they do not exist at the base and are introduced by this change), and the MCP consumers are ROUTED THROUGH those new resolvers, which is where ambient config/secret reads are legitimately owned. This PRESERVES the exact per-request semantics the MCP gate/auth docstrings promise (no per-request->startup-frozen change) — there is NO behavioral delta. The MCP `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries are removed. `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` reports zero findings for these paths with those entries gone and no path-glob exception. The subsystem's behavioral suites stay green, unmodified.\n\n## Plan\n1. Add three new owned composition-root resolvers to `config.py` (which is already a composition root): `mcp_gate(attr, *, fail)` (typed bool gate, fail-closed on ConfigError), `compose_config() -> Config` (process-root config entry), and `read_secret_env(env_name) -> str` (secret VALUE resolved at the boundary, in-memory only, \"\" on unset/empty). These do not exist at the base; this change introduces them.\n2. Route the below-seam `load_config()` calls (`mcp_server.py` L422/591/735) and the auth-secret `os.environ.get` reads (`_mcp_auth.py` L411/658/760, `mcp_server.py` L646) through the new `config.py` resolvers (`mcp_gate`/`compose_config`/`read_secret_env`), so the consumers RECEIVE composed config/secret values from the composition root instead of reading ambient config/env below the seam. Per-request resolution semantics are preserved (no startup freeze); secret VALUES stay in-memory only and fail-closed on unset/empty is unchanged.\n3. Remove the corresponding MCP entries from `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` in `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`.\n4. Run `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and the subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/facades MCP suites, tests/unit MCP/auth suites); keep green.\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Held-out test `tests/scripts/test_mcp_server_seam_clean_heldout.py` asserts `check_config_ownership.check(check_config_ownership.REPO_ROOT)` returns no finding string containing any of the listed paths, AND that `config_ownership_exceptions.LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` contains zero entries whose `path` is one of the listed files. RED now (entries present + reads below seam).\n- The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/facades MCP suites, tests/unit MCP/auth suites) stay green after the cutover — they are the correctness oracle the AST gate supplements.\n- No behavioral delta: the MCP/auth behavioral suites (179 tests) pass UNMODIFIED before and after the cutover.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nNo stored ticket/event/binding format changes. The new `config.py` resolvers are additive; the cutover is a pure routing change with no behavioral delta, so rollback is reverting the single change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No direct ambient config/credential read, backend reload, or configurable default remains below the approved seam in the 2 listed MCP files; each is cut-to-seam through the new owned `config.py` resolvers.\n- [x] The `LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS` entries for these files are removed from `scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py`, and `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` passes with no path-glob exception (proven by the held-out `test_mcp_server_seam_clean_heldout.py`).\n- [x] The subsystem behavioral suites (tests/interfaces/facades MCP suites, tests/unit MCP/auth suites) pass after the cutover, unmodified; there is no behavioral delta (per-request semantics preserved).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/config.py","reason":"Owned composition-root resolvers (mcp_gate/compose_config/read_secret_env) that supply composed config/secrets to the MCP consumers."},{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"Cut below-seam load_config/os.environ reads to the config.py resolvers."},{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py","reason":"Cut below-seam auth-secret os.environ reads to read_secret_env; dropped import os."},{"path":"scripts/config_ownership_exceptions.py","reason":"Removed the 3 C3e LEGACY_EXCEPTIONS entries as the reads are cut to seam."},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"Regenerated for the relocated reads."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_mcp_server_seam_clean_heldout.py","reason":"Held-out proof: gate clean + zero legacy entries for the MCP files."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","075b-1479-dcb7-40ab"],["relates_to","59ce-3ff1-b46a-4d8b"],["relates_to","b464-181d-0ecb-45b9"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"075b-1479-dcb7-40ab","parent_status_uuid":"478803c9-a2a6-4700-9c73-eba601814991","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9e42-78f7-c164-4bc8","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.3.e — mcp-server cutover: route below-seam config reads through seams","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7a98d51c-c20f-46df-a2b0-3acf382d0e73","478803c9-a2a6-4700-9c73-eba601814991","2716028e-405a-4890-9755-7edcff27bfe5","10ad9d6b-a740-4a8b-b219-e855fe4de80c","1df0ae3e-2e1e-47ed-9195-ebfbbb0dc840","0411c164-1dee-46be-aa14-4b875ef0c46e","b3fd1d5d-0ebf-48e6-bbf6-8337e6eba1b2","5437fbca-e7cc-4375-b1be-4d362a1440e5","afdbf58d-cf10-4e4a-9274-2d645f80186f","e0eda35f-49c8-422f-9b0b-ac9dfaf18a80","3ee57c48-5945-48ec-88c5-7879d922812d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787103625079113002,"uuid":"3625e047-b4bb-43c3-98